  "result": {
    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Separation makes logistic regression fail loudly in the warnings and quietly in the estimates\"\ndescription: \"As a predictor gets closer to perfectly separating a binary outcome, the maximum likelihood estimate diverges. R warns about fitted probabilities, not about the coefficient — which is the number people actually report.\"\ndate: 2026-08-12\ncategories:\n  - stats-cases\nengine: knitr\n---\n\nWhen a predictor separates a binary outcome perfectly, the logistic regression\nmaximum likelihood estimate does not exist. The likelihood keeps increasing as\nthe coefficient grows, so the optimiser stops at whatever its convergence rule\nhappens to hit. The reported number is an artefact of the stopping rule.\n\nR does warn, but it warns about the wrong thing: `fitted probabilities\nnumerically 0 or 1 occurred` describes a symptom on the probability scale. The\ncoefficient and its standard error — the two numbers that end up in a table —\ncome back with no annotation at all.\n\nThis post simulates the approach to separation so you can watch both quantities\ngo.\n\n## Setup\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(ggplot2)\nlibrary(ggiraph)\nlibrary(plotly)\n\nset.seed(20260812)\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Simulating the approach to separation\n\nOne predictor, one binary outcome. The parameter `beta` controls how sharply\nthe outcome tracks the predictor: at `beta = 0.5` the classes overlap heavily,\nand as `beta` grows the boundary sharpens until — in any finite sample — the\ntwo classes stop overlapping at all. That last state is separation, and it\narrives by degrees rather than all at once.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nsimulate_once <- function(beta, n = 200) {\n  x <- rnorm(n)\n  y <- rbinom(n, size = 1, prob = plogis(beta * x))\n  data.frame(x = x, y = y)\n}\n\n# `glm` warns about fitted probabilities near separation; that warning is the\n# subject of this post rather than a problem with the call, so it is captured\n# rather than printed 40 times.\nfit_once <- function(beta) {\n  d <- simulate_once(beta)\n  warned <- FALSE\n  m <- withCallingHandlers(\n    glm(y ~ x, data = d, family = binomial),\n    warning = function(w) {\n      warned <<- TRUE\n      invokeRestart(\"muffleWarning\")\n    }\n  )\n  co <- summary(m)$coefficients\n  overlap <- min(max(d$x[d$y == 0]), max(d$x[d$y == 1])) -\n    max(min(d$x[d$y == 0]), min(d$x[d$y == 1]))\n\n  data.frame(\n    beta_true = beta,\n    estimate  = co[\"x\", \"Estimate\"],\n    se        = co[\"x\", \"Std. Error\"],\n    warned    = warned,\n    overlap   = overlap\n  )\n}\n\nbetas <- seq(0.5, 18, length.out = 45)\nres <- do.call(rbind, lapply(betas, fit_once))\n```\n:::\n\n\n## The estimate\n\nHover any point for the fitted values. Points where R issued a warning are\nmarked.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nres$tooltip <- sprintf(\n  \"true beta: %.1f\\nestimate: %.2f\\nstd. error: %.2f\\nR warned: %s\",\n  res$beta_true, res$estimate, res$se, ifelse(res$warned, \"yes\", \"no\")\n)\n\np <- ggplot(res, aes(beta_true, estimate)) +\n  geom_abline(slope = 1, intercept = 0, linetype = \"dashed\", colour = \"grey55\") +\n  geom_line(colour = \"grey70\") +\n  geom_point_interactive(\n    aes(tooltip = tooltip, data_id = beta_true, colour = warned),\n    size = 2.8\n  ) +\n  scale_colour_manual(\n    values = c(\"FALSE\" = \"#0f766e\", \"TRUE\" = \"#b45309\"),\n    labels = c(\"FALSE\" = \"no warning\", \"TRUE\" = \"R warned\"),\n    name = NULL\n  ) +\n  labs(x = \"true coefficient\", y = \"estimated coefficient\") +\n  theme_minimal(base_size = 13) +\n  theme(legend.position = \"top\")\n\ngirafe(\n  ggobj = p,\n  width_svg = 7,\n  height_svg = 4.2,\n  options = list(\n    opts_hover(css = \"fill:#c026d3;stroke:none;r:5pt;\"),\n    opts_tooltip(css = \"background:#111;color:#eee;padding:6px;border-radius:4px;font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;\")\n  )\n)\n```\n\n::: {#fig-estimates .cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"girafe html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-7d23dbe305b18d378582\" style=\"width:100%;height:417px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-7d23dbe305b18d378582\">{\"x\":{\"html\":\"<?xml version=\\\"1.0\\\" encoding=\\\"UTF-8\\\"?>\\n<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' xmlns:xlink='http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink' class='ggiraph-svg' role='graphics-document' id='svg_4446946974015584' viewBox='0 0 504 302.4'>\\n <defs id='svg_4446946974015584_defs'>\\n  <clipPath id='svg_4446946974015584_c1'>\\n   <rect x='0' y='0' width='504' height='302.4'/>\\n  <\\/clipPath>\\n  <clipPath id='svg_4446946974015584_c2'>\\n   <rect x='38.75' y='49.66' width='458.77' height='216.25'/>\\n  <\\/clipPath>\\n <\\/defs>\\n <g id='svg_4446946974015584_rootg' class='ggiraph-svg-rootg'>\\n  <g clip-path='url(#svg_4446946974015584_c1)'>\\n   <rect x='0' y='0' width='504' height='302.4' fill='#FFFFFF' fill-opacity='1' stroke='#FFFFFF' stroke-opacity='1' stroke-width='0.75' stroke-linejoin='round' stroke-linecap='round' class='ggiraph-svg-bg'/>\\n   <rect x='0' y='0' width='504' height='302.4' fill='#FFFFFF' fill-opacity='1' stroke='none'/>\\n  <\\/g>\\n  <g clip-path='url(#svg_4446946974015584_c2)'>\\n   <polyline points='38.75,237.76 497.52,237.76' fill='none' stroke='#EBEBEB' stroke-opacity='1' stroke-width='0.63' stroke-linejoin='round' stroke-linecap='butt'/>\\n   <polyline points='38.75,197.31 497.52,197.31' fill='none' stroke='#EBEBEB' stroke-opacity='1' stroke-width='0.63' stroke-linejoin='round' stroke-linecap='butt'/>\\n   <polyline points='38.75,156.87 497.52,156.87' fill='none' stroke='#EBEBEB' stroke-opacity='1' stroke-width='0.63' stroke-linejoin='round' stroke-linecap='butt'/>\\n   <polyline points='38.75,116.42 497.52,116.42' fill='none' stroke='#EBEBEB' stroke-opacity='1' stroke-width='0.63' stroke-linejoin='round' stroke-linecap='butt'/>\\n   <polyline points='38.75,75.97 497.52,75.97' fill='none' stroke='#EBEBEB' stroke-opacity='1' stroke-width=